   "text": "I read the structure as a maleimide\u2013PEG\u2013amide linker on a central tertiary amide nitrogen. Two identical arms branch from that nitrogen, and each arm carries a glucuronide-protected benzofuran linked to an MMAE-type payload. I wrote the SMILES by region and then checked the stereocentres against CIP descriptors.\n\n**Linker core**\n- The maleimide N is attached to CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013N.\n- That amide N carries two CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013 arms, each ending on C4 of a 1,2,3-triazole.\n\n**Each arm**\n- Triazole N1 \u2192 CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2CH2\u2013, attached to C2 of a benzofuran.\n- Benzofuran C4 carries O\u2011\u03b2\u2011D\u2011glucuronic acid. Benzofuran C7 carries CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)\u2013, a carbamate onto the payload.\n\n**Payload (MMAE-type)**\n- N\u2011Me\u2011Val, then Val, then N\u2011Me dolaisoleuine (sec-butyl, OMe), then pyrrolidine (dolaproine OMe, methyl), then amide to the (1S,2R)\u20111\u2011hydroxy\u20111\u2011phenylpropan\u20112\u2011yl (norephedrine) group.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Both valines are L.\n- Dolaisoleuine is 3R,4S,5S.\n- The pyrrolidine C\u03b1 is S.\n- The dolaproine OMe carbon and its methyl carbon are R,R.\n- Norephedrine is 1S,2R.\n- The glucuronide is the \u03b2\u2011D form.\n- I recalled the MMAE SMILES from memory and found its norephedrine C2 to be S, not R, so I rechecked each centre. I confirmed norephedrine C2 as R from the wedge geometry in the image, and the other centres from the CIP descriptors above.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCOCCOCC(=O)N(CCOCc2cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc3cc4c(O[C@@H]5O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]5O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N7CCC[C@H]7[C@H](OC)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@H](C)[C@H](c8ccccc8)O)c4o3)nn2)CCOCc2cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc3cc4c(O[C@@H]5O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]5O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C